From 2a10cf4dbee63dbf79f82b1d3ae685cbc0563730 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AlexanderNyr <131390634+AlexanderNyr@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 16:29:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] PERF P0: measure executed work before optimizing

Add an opt-in --stats count of cpu_step done-path attempts, distinct from the K3/K6 guest clock (which charges +512 on all-idle HLT slots). The shared machine_executed_total handles historical n_vcpus=0 and the SMP slot. Six unit vectors pin the clock/work divergence, faults, K6 identity, context summation and cap independence.

Add a seven-tape, repeated, median host-wall bench (separate always-built O2 binary so the sanitizer target cannot silently contaminate results). Gate deterministic work accounting, nonzero work and the cap not being reached; never gate a fixed host timing. The one P0 negative control uses the cap as the numerator and fails, with 10.34x inflation on the firmware boot tape.

Measured: make test RC=0; make test-sanitize RC=0; make fuzz FUZZ_PROGRAMS=256 RC=0 (256 programs, 6144 instructions, all states match, zero host crashes); make bench BENCH_REPS=3 RC=0; make bench-nc BENCH_REPS=3 RC=2 (inner recipe RC=1, FAILED AS DESIGNED). Four historical pre/post firmware/video tape stdout/log/PPM pairs are byte-identical without --stats. Guest toolchain unavailable; frozen-guest lanes SKIP. See docs/plans/PERF_PLAN.md and same-phase CHANGELOG/ROADMAP/STATUS.
